From 04f0ba25c0a5e13fca1ad1bdbcf4b8c9ab796e6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teal Bauer <teal@starsong.eu>
Date: Tue, 3 Mar 2026 16:08:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add FBDEV display backend

Upstream-Status: Pending

Add a new FBDEV backend type that decouples GPU rendering from display
output. Renders via EGL/GLES on a render node (/dev/dri/renderD128)
using GBM surfaces, then blits rendered frames to /dev/fb0 via memcpy.

This avoids all DRM modesetting (drmModeSetCrtc/drmModePageFlip),
making it suitable for hardware where the GPU and display controller
are separate devices (e.g. i.MX6 with etnaviv GPU + IPU display).

Key components:
- NativeWindowFbdev: render node + fbdev display, ARGB8888->RGB565
- ELinuxWindowFbdev: libinput handling without DRM udev monitoring
- CMake FBDEV backend type with proper dependency resolution

Environment variables:
  FLUTTER_FB_DEVICE=/dev/fb0
  FLUTTER_EGL_DEVICE=/dev/dri/renderD128
